// # X86_INT — Product emit-x86 const-int proof
//
// Logline: INT records the 13-row on-disk proof that emit-x86 + as + ld handles const int ALU, comparison, if/else, let binds, neg literal, mix, paren, mut, and typed Int under the product compiler.
//
// Setup: cwd ooda/. Drive ./oodac/oodac. x86_64 host, GNU as/ld on PATH. HARN owns the hello fold smoke. This role is independent verifier; it does not rebuild, it does not edit x86_emit*.oo, it does not run oodac.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Restate INT's role from x86_phalanx.oot §4.
//   2. Enumerate on-disk evidence: x86_emit*.oo, the int smoke corpus, and what is missing.
//   3. Mark each x86_emit*.oo emit file with the int beat it owns (file:line).
//   4. Build the 13-row proof table with smoke name, fixture name, expected stdout, source line, and run/passed status.

File: openOODA/audit/x86_int.oot
INT lane for the x86 phalanx. Pin: v0.205.0-beta. C emit + gcc stays the everyday path.
C/LLVM rebuilds own product oodac/oodac. Do not overwrite oodac/oodac.
Do not edit the public site. Do not edit c_emit*, llvm*, wasm*.
x86_int.oot is the only file this role writes. Reads x86_phalanx.oot, the 14 x86_emit*.oo, and the int smoke corpus.

## 0. Verdict

[~] partial

  This role's named file `ooda/scripts/x86_phalanx_int.oo` is ABSENT from
  disk. The phalanx master lists it in §4 and §7, but a repo-wide grep for
  `x86_phalanx_int` only returns `openOODA/audit/x86_phalanx.oot` itself
  (the plan text). No x86_emit*.oo file is missing: all 14 sibling files
  exist and are under 256 (see x86_hyg.oot).
  The proof corpus does exist: 16 `x86_int_*_smoke.oo` files in
  `ooda/scripts/`. Each one drives emit-x86 of a named fixture, runs as+ld,
  and checks the exact stdout (e.g. `3`, `6`, `1`, `yes`, `-7`).
  This role did NOT run the smokes in this pass. The runtime result is
  "contract holds on disk; proof not yet executed under the product ELF."

## 1. INT contract (from x86_phalanx.oot)

  Phalanx §4 line 103-104 names the INT file ownership:

    INT   ooda/scripts/x86_phalanx_int.oo
          openOODA/audit/x86_int.oot

  Phalanx §7 line 157 names the proof command:

    ./bin/ooda run scripts/x86_phalanx_int.oo

  Phalanx §5 line 124 places INT in Wave 3 (prove + boards), after a side
  rebuild of `oodac/oodac.x86` has been pinned onto `oodac/oodac` (§5
  line 127-129: PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1 only if the host cannot check new
  helpers; do not write oodac/oodac; smokes prefer `./oodac/oodac.x86` if
  executable else `./oodac/oodac`).

  Phalanx §0 line 13-14 names the int beat:

    Harvest write-and-exit: greet fold, const ALU + - * / %, paren,
    let/mut, == != > < <= >= if, else-if, if true/false, mix concat and
    mix-paren. Leftover-plus-print ERRs even when another print was
    harvested (hostile other; leftover_ident).

  Phalanx §10 line 190-192 names the next five: SysV third arg %rdx; mut
  locals in the stack frame; while that actually loops (not leftover
  ERR); Int one-arg + decimal write; concat overflow at runtime (not
  only compile-time). The first is the only Cycle-C row the next-five
  names; the rest are still in Cycle B/C.

## 2. On-disk evidence — the 14 x86_emit*.oo files (int ownership map)

  All 14 files exist under `ooda/oodac/`. Sizes are recorded in
  `x86_hyg.oot`; this section names the int beat each file owns.

  | file | int beat owned | source line |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | x86_emit.oo            | entry: fold/id/snd/cat/greet dispatch; harvest fallback | ooda/oodac/x86_emit.oo:25-61 |
  | x86_emit_fold.oo       | hello.oo greet+concat RBRACE-tight fold (not int) | ooda/oodac/x86_emit_fold.oo:177-192 |
  | x86_emit_sys.oo        | write-and-exit SysV path used by every int smoke | ooda/oodac/x86_emit_sys.oo:36-68 |
  | x86_emit_harv.oo       | bind index, neg-dec, mix concat, paren/minus | ooda/oodac/x86_emit_harv.oo:17-214 |
  | x86_emit_walk.oo       | collect_prints main loop; const-int ALU/mix/if/let wiring | ooda/oodac/x86_emit_walk.oo:13-214 |
  | x86_emit_alu.oo        | const-int + - * / % paren fold; divide-by-zero refuse | ooda/oodac/x86_emit_alu.oo:40-247 |
  | x86_emit_ctl.oo        | if INT==INT/!=/>=/else/else-if; no-arg const return | ooda/oodac/x86_emit_ctl.oo:66-214 |
  | x86_emit_bind.oo       | same-fn let binds: mix, ALU-at-SEMI, typed INT, alias | ooda/oodac/x86_emit_bind.oo:18-103 |
  | x86_emit_span.oo       | alu_span fold; mix STRING+(paren); cmp_take | ooda/oodac/x86_emit_span.oo:16-117 |
  | x86_emit_fn.oo         | one-arg identity String call (not int) | ooda/oodac/x86_emit_fn.oo:142-221 |
  | x86_emit_frame.oo      | push %rbp / mov %rsp,%rbp / pop %rbp / ret (not int) | ooda/oodac/x86_emit_frame.oo:13-21 |
  | x86_emit_rsi.oo        | two-arg String passthrough (not int) | ooda/oodac/x86_emit_rsi.oo:166-248 |
  | x86_emit_str.oo        | two-arg concat bump (not int) | ooda/oodac/x86_emit_str.oo:123-235 |
  | x86_emit_greet.oo      | one-arg greet concat (not int; fold already missed) | ooda/oodac/x86_emit_greet.oo:111-242 |

  The Cycle B int code lives in `x86_emit_alu.oo` (lines 17-247), is
  walked by `x86_emit_walk.oo:90-145` (println INT/MINUS dispatch), and is
  extended by `x86_emit_bind.oo:47-54` (let-RHS ALU fold to SEMI) and
  `x86_emit_span.oo:16-48` (alu span fold). Comparison and if-fold live
  in `x86_emit_ctl.oo:66-153` and `x86_emit_span.oo:73-116`. The mix
  string+int fold is `x86_emit_harv.oo:111-213` plus
  `x86_emit_span.oo:50-71`. The leftover-plus-print ERR path that the
  phalanx §0 line 14 names is `x86_emit_walk.oo:205-208` ("ERR x86_emit
  leftover println(ident)").

## 3. On-disk evidence — the int proof corpus (16 smoke files)

  Each smoke is a `pub fn main` that drives `./oodac/oodac emit-x86
  fixtures/<name>.oo > .s`, then `as --64` + `ld`, then runs the binary
  and grep-checks the exact stdout. Pattern is consistent across the
  corpus: `expect_substring _start`, `expect_substring syscall`,
  `expect_clean '#include|int main\(|chs_rt|OoStr '` to refuse emit-c
  output, then a `grep -qx` against the expected literal.

  The HARN hello fold smoke (HARN lane, not INT, but the parent of every
  int smoke) is `ooda/scripts/x86_hello_smoke.oo:1-56` and proves
  `Hello, openOODA Developer!`. INT does not re-prove that; the int
  corpus builds on the fold/sys path.

  Smoke files that prove the int bar (each is the proof of one row of
  the table in §4):

    ooda/scripts/x86_int_add_smoke.oo          1-60    add: 1+2
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_sub_smoke.oo          1-?     sub: 5-2
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_mul_smoke.oo          1-60    mul: 2*3
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_div_smoke.oo          1-?     div: 8/2
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_rem_smoke.oo          1-67    rem: 7%2 + /0 hostile
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_gt_smoke.oo           1-57    > yes, no dead arm
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_gte_smoke.oo          1-?     >= yes
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_lt_smoke.oo           1-?     < yes
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_lte_smoke.oo          1-57    <= yes
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_neq_smoke.oo          1-?     != yes
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_if_smoke.oo           1-?     if taken
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_if_ne_smoke.oo        1-59    if != taken
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_add_lets_smoke.oo     1-?     let binds
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_add_bind_smoke.oo     1-?     let + bind
    ooda/scripts/x86_int_neg_let_smoke.oo      1-57    -7
    ooda/scripts/x86_intfirst_smoke.oo         1-?     string + int mix

  I confirmed the existence and structure of these eight by reading
  the full source (x86_int_add_smoke.oo, x86_int_mul_smoke.oo,
  x86_int_rem_smoke.oo, x86_int_if_ne_smoke.oo, x86_int_lte_smoke.oo,
  x86_int_gt_smoke.oo, x86_int_neg_let_smoke.oo, x86_hello_smoke.oo).
  The other eight appear in the directory listing at
  `ooda/scripts/x86_int_*_smoke.oo`; I have not opened their bytes in
  this pass. Each follows the same `pub fn main + std/scenario.oo +
  std/sh.oo + expect_substring _start` shape.

