  | # | beat | smoke | fixture | expected stdout | source line | run? | pass? |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  |  1 | const ALU +       | x86_int_add_smoke.oo    | x86_int_add.oo    | 3  | ooda/scripts/x86_int_add_smoke.oo:44 | [?] not run | [?] not run |
  |  2 | const ALU -       | x86_int_sub_smoke.oo    | x86_int_sub.oo    | 3  | ooda/scripts/x86_int_sub_smoke.oo:? | [?] not run | [?] not run |
  |  3 | const ALU *       | x86_int_mul_smoke.oo    | x86_int_mul.oo    | 6  | ooda/scripts/x86_int_mul_smoke.oo:44 | [?] not run | [?] not run |
  |  4 | const ALU /       | x86_int_div_smoke.oo    | x86_int_div.oo    | 4  | ooda/scripts/x86_int_div_smoke.oo:? | [?] not run | [?] not run |
  |  5 | const ALU % + /0  | x86_int_rem_smoke.oo    | x86_int_rem.oo    | 1  | ooda/scripts/x86_int_rem_smoke.oo:41 | [?] not run | [?] not run |
  |  6 | const if == taken | x86_int_if_smoke.oo     | x86_int_if.oo     | yes | ooda/scripts/x86_int_if_smoke.oo:? | [?] not run | [?] not run |
  |  7 | const if != taken | x86_int_if_ne_smoke.oo  | x86_int_if_ne.oo  | yes | ooda/scripts/x86_int_if_ne_smoke.oo:43 | [?] not run | [?] not run |
  |  8 | const > if        | x86_int_gt_smoke.oo     | x86_int_gt.oo     | yes | ooda/scripts/x86_int_gt_smoke.oo:41 | [?] not run | [?] not run |
  |  9 | const <= if       | x86_int_lte_smoke.oo    | x86_int_lte.oo    | yes | ooda/scripts/x86_int_lte_smoke.oo:41 | [?] not run | [?] not run |
  | 10 | let bind ALU      | x86_int_add_lets_smoke.oo | x86_int_add_lets.oo | 6  | ooda/scripts/x86_int_add_lets_smoke.oo:? | [?] not run | [?] not run |
  | 11 | let bind typed    | x86_int_add_bind_smoke.oo | x86_int_add_bind.oo | 6  | ooda/scripts/x86_int_add_bind_smoke.oo:? | [?] not run | [?] not run |
  | 12 | negative literal  | x86_int_neg_let_smoke.oo | x86_int_neg_let.oo | -7 | ooda/scripts/x86_int_neg_let_smoke.oo:41 | [?] not run | [?] not run |
  | 13 | mix string+int    | x86_intfirst_smoke.oo   | x86_intfirst.oo   | "x"+3=... | ooda/scripts/x86_intfirst_smoke.oo:? | [?] not run | [?] not run |

  Three rows have a `?` source line because the smoke exists in
  `ooda/scripts/x86_int_*_smoke.oo` per the directory listing but I have
  not opened its bytes this pass. Rows 1, 3, 5, 7, 8, 9, 12 are
  fully-cited because I did read those seven smoke files in full. Row
  4 /0 path is enforced by `x86_int_rem_smoke.oo:60-65` (rem0 fixture
  emits with no `_start` and an `ERR x86_emit x86 buf` style line; the
  actual line is the `process_exit(1)` arm of `x86_emit_alu.oo:88-90`
  for `/` and `x86_emit_alu.oo:92-95` for `%`). The hostile
  "leftover-plus-print" case in phalanx §0 line 14 is the
  `x86_emit_walk.oo:205-208` ERR exit; the corresponding smoke is
  `x86_leftover_ident_smoke.oo` and `x86_hostile_leftover_smoke.oo`
  (not in the int 13, but they are the leftover ERRs the phalanx
  promises).

